        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Adams Rite 4565 Deadlatch Handle</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nDesigned to operate 4900 Series Deadlatches by a natural downward hand movement, these handles incorporate an activator cam plug that mounts on the handles' escutcheon and fits solidly into the cylinder hole of the latch. Not intended for use as a door pull.  The Adams Rite 4565 handles feature a thumbturn of minimum practical length.  Ideal for doors where the latch is operated infrequently.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nCam Plug: Furnished for use with 4900 Series Deadlatches. Secured in latch body by cylinder set screw, plug is also rigidly tied to escutcheon by hardened steel pins\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nEscutcheons: A 1/4\" [6.4 mm] square heat-treated spindle is part of escutcheon assembly, which interlocks with the cam plug. Finished to match lever.</li>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Adams Rite 4590 Deadlatch Paddle:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Handle Material: Cast aluminum</li>\r\n<li>Operating assembly: Steel mechanism</li>\r\n<li>Thumbturn Length: 1.9\"</li>\r\n<li>Escutcheon Height: 4\"</li>\r\n<li>Escutcheon Width: 1-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Projection: 1-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Finish: Aluminum</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<i>Special Ordered Item. <b>NO RETURNS</b></i>\r\n</p>",
